Myth: In the dawn before structure, existence sprawled without distinction—everything touching everything, no boundary between self and other, thought and action, dream and waking. The world suffocated in its own unity.

A potter named Kael wandered this formless expanse, carrying clay that somehow remained separate from the chaos. She noticed the clay held different textures—some smooth as possibility, others rough as limit, still others marked with the grooves of definition.

